🇷🇺 Lavrov: Russia Sees Strong Prospects for BRICS Cooperation in the Arctic

Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov, in an article published on the Arctic.ru portal, stated:

➡️Russia has good prospects for cooperation with BRICS countries in the Far North;

➡️Numerous foreign delegations will discuss Arctic issues at the Eastern Economic Forum on September 1;

➡️South Korea and Singapore are interested in working with Russia on select Arctic projects, despite participating in Western sanctions;

➡️NATO's military activity in the Far North raises the risk of incidents with catastrophic consequences;

➡️NATO is conducting intensified military preparations near Russia's northern borders;

➡️NATO wants to turn the Arctic into a new front for containing the development of Russia and its allies;

➡️Russia will respond to hostile actions by its opponents, including asymmetrically;

➡️Russia is ready to resume full-fledged activity of the Arctic Council, provided others work in good faith.

